----- stdout -----
Export recorded audit events to a sink

Usage: auditstream export [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --config <PATH>
          Path to the configuration file (defaults to ./auditstream.toml if present)
          
          [env: AUDITSTREAM_CONFIG=]

      --format <FORMAT>
          Destination encoding (default: jsonl)
          
          [possible values: jsonl, csv]

      --database-url <URL>
          Postgres connection URL (also reads `DATABASE_URL` as fallback)
          
          [env: AUDITSTREAM_DATABASE_URL]

      --output <PATH>
          Append to this file (default: stdout)

      --cursor-file <PATH>
          Persist the last acknowledged position and resume on the next run

      --schema <SCHEMA>
          Audit schema name (defaults to `auditstream`)
          
          [env: AUDITSTREAM_SCHEMA=]

      --batch-size <N>
          Maximum events per batch (default: 1000)

  -v, --verbose...
          Increase log verbosity (`-v` info, `-vv` debug)

      --from-start
          Replay from the beginning and replace the stored cursor

  -q, --quiet
          Silence warnings and info logs (errors only)

      --allow-rls-filtered
          Allow exporting when Row-Level Security filters rows on `<schema>.changes` (for intentional per-tenant exports)

      --log-format <LOG_FORMAT>
          Format for stderr log messages

          Possible values:
          - text: Human-readable plain text logs (default)
          - json: Structured single-line JSON log records on stderr
          
          [env: AUDITSTREAM_LOG_FORMAT=]
          [default: text]

      --stats-format <STATS_FORMAT>
          Format for the stderr summary (`text` or `json`; defaults to `json` with `--log-format json`, else `text`)

          Possible values:
          - text: Human-readable single-line summary on stderr (default)
          - json: Structured single-line JSON telemetry summary on stderr

      --since <TIME>
          Include events at or after this RFC 3339 timestamp or UTC date

      --until <TIME>
          Include events strictly before this RFC 3339 timestamp or UTC date

      --actor <ID>
          Match an actor ID directly or through onBehalfOf

      --tenant <ID>
          Match a tenant ID directly or through onBehalfOf

      --source <db|app>
          Select database changes or application events

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

----- stderr -----
